      ":question/problem": "Consider the change of variables given by the matrix equation\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$,\nand the curve $C$, defined as\n$C: 5x_{1}^{2} - 4x_{1}x_{2} + 5x_{2}^{2} - 2x_{1} + 2x_{2} = \\frac{145}{7}$.\n\nGiven that the change of variables above reduces $Q(x) = 5x_{1}^{2} - 4x_{1}x_{2} + 5x_{2}^{2}$ to its canonical (diagonal) form $7y_{1}^{2} + 3y_{2}^{2}$, what type of a quadratic curve is defined by $C$?"
